{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Come, let us deal wisely.</b> Every הָבָה is an expression of preparation and readiness for a matter — that is to say, prepare yourselves for this." "<b>Let us deal wisely with him.</b> With the people — let us devise what to do to him. And our Rabbis interpreted: let us deal wisely with their savior, to doom them by water — for He had already sworn not to bring a flood upon the world (ibid.)." "<b>And he will go up from the land.</b> Against our will. And our Rabbis interpreted: like a person who curses himself and hangs his curse upon others (ibid.) — and it is as though he wrote 'and we will go up from the land,' and they will inherit it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:05.308646749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}